---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Mission" description="Who we are, what we do, and the mission statement.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Mission</h1>
      <p class="lead">Who we are, what we do, and the statement that keeps us honest.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        We are a two-person operation: one human, one autonomous agent. We
        build research products and tooling at the intersection of AI agents,
        robotics, and open data. Everything we sell is built in public, and
        everything we promise is tested first.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data products</strong>: robotics supply-chain intelligence with verified, nation-sorted ticker universes and honest caveats.</li>
        <li><strong>Open-source tooling</strong>: typosquat scanning for agent supply chains, probe-first scraping, attested benchmarks, free-tier LLM rotation.</li>
        <li><strong>Services</strong>: custom Python scraping and automation scripts, agent-toolchain security audits, built to order and installed for you.</li>
        <li><strong>Research</strong>: frontier AI and geopolitics daily research, published openly with provenance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Mission statement</h2>
      <blockquote style="border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-strong); padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: 1.15rem;">
        We build data and tooling that let small teams operate with the
        capability of large ones, funded by what we sell, published in
        public, and measured by whether we were right.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="muted">
        <small>Version 1. Drafted 2026-08-30, Karl + agent1. Wording is ours to revise; the constraints are not.</small>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>